{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480762-is-anyone-else-weirded-out-by-the-current-resonance-rules","id":1480762,"title":"Is anyone else weirded out by the current resonance rules?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-05-11T13:45:57-07:00","id":1480762,"title":"Is anyone else weirded out by the current resonance rules?","content":"Under the current rules, Resonance is largely a punishment.<br /> <br /> Players don't really get to choose what resonance they have or how strong it becomes after character generation, Resonance makes characters monumentally easier to track and identify by tainting everything the touch or do with magic, and the only supposed &quot;benefit&quot; is the ability to add dice to 1 role Once per story(not session). I know the concept of resonance Started as the echoes flaw, but after all the iterations it's been through that doesn't mean it should still be something as damaging as a 5 point flaw.<br /> <br /> This is especially weird to me because resonance is a system that's easy to balance from a mechanical standpoint. In previous versions, any benefits resonance gave you in one task became a penalty to another task, and trying to decrease that penalty resulted in decreasing the benefits as well.<br /> <br /> Take a Healing resonance for example. If a mage gained a difficulty or dice bonus for healing/restoration/building stuff magic from that resonance, then they'd gain an equal dice or difficulty Penalty in destructive/painful/changing magics(which would be very inconvenient for things like combat). You could go very crazy without it becoming overpowered because it's a self-balancing system.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, the current rules throw the mechanics of that out, but tries to hold onto the fluff, which we don't need resonance for. If I wanted to describe a building as dark and scary, I don't need to fill out a 4 dot resonance trait to do that. I can just describe it in a way that conveys that it's dark and scary.<br /> <br /> Is there something I'm not seeing? Can others provide a different perspective on this?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6383,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","user":"Prometheas","date":". 05-11-2022, 04:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-11T16:25:37-07:00","id":1480773,"title":"","content":"I think you're right. Making characters more trackable on a constant basis for a very occasional benefit is punitive. I've been wondering about an exception to the rule. Suppose a player most often uses their magic specifically to avoid detection. Shouldn't the resulting Resonance make them <i>less</i> trackable?<br /> <br /> An example would be a Life 2, Correspondence 2, Mind 2, Entropy 2 effect, anchored to the Mage's Life Pattern, that deflects attention onto some other random person. Under RAW, if they used this frequently, which of the four Resonance types would it cause them to develop? Every extra die added also makes the Mage <i>more</i> detectable, overall.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-12T05:42:41-07:00","id":1480824,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HorizonParty2021</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480762-is-anyone-else-weirded-out-by-the-current-resonance-rules?p=1480773#post1480773\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think you're right. Making characters more trackable on a constant basis for a very occasional benefit is punitive. I've been wondering about an exception to the rule. Suppose a player most often uses their magic specifically to avoid detection. Shouldn't the resulting Resonance make them <i>less</i> trackable?<br /> <br /> An example would be a Life 2, Correspondence 2, Mind 2, Entropy 2 effect, anchored to the Mage's Life Pattern, that deflects attention onto some other random person. Under RAW, if they used this frequently, which of the four Resonance types would it cause them to develop? Every extra die added also makes the Mage <i>more</i> detectable, overall.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Gotta love being caught because your <i>Sneaky </i>3 and <i>Undetectable</i> 4 resonances revealed your location.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}